-- title:
--   Abhyankar's lemma on completions at a regular surface point
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a regular local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by two elements $\varpi, s$ and whose Krull dimension is $2$, and let $e$ be a positive integer whose image in $O$ is a unit. Let $C$ be an $O$-algebra which is a domain, module-finite over $O$ and with $O \to C$ injective, and let $\mathfrak n \subset C$ be a maximal ideal lying over $\mathfrak m_O$. Let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $C$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $O$-action, such that every $G$-invariant element of $C$ lies in the image of $O$. Assume that the inertia subgroup of $\mathfrak n$ in $G$, regarded as a subgroup of the stabiliser of $\mathfrak n$, has cardinality $e$, that the inertia subgroup of $\mathfrak n$ in $G$ is cyclic, and that the residue extension $O/\mathfrak m_O \to C/\mathfrak n$ is separable. Let $S$ be a local ring which is a localisation of $C$ at $\mathfrak n$, an $O$-algebra compatibly with $O \to C \to S$, and assume the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic completion of $S$ is an integrally closed domain. Assume finally that $S$ is unramified over $O$ at every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $S$ which is not maximal and whose contraction to $O$ does not contain $s$. Then there exist a regular local ring $R'$ of Krull dimension $2$, elements $\varpi', \tau$ generating $\mathfrak m_{R'}$, and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic completion of $S$ onto the $\mathfrak m_{R'}$-adic completion of $R'$ carrying the image of $\varpi$ to the image of $\varpi'$.
--
--   This is a form of Abhyankar's lemma at a regular two-dimensional point, stated on completions: tame cyclic inertia of order $e$ together with unramifiedness away from the divisor $s = 0$ forces the completion of the local ring at $\mathfrak n$ to be the completion of a regular two-dimensional local ring in which the pulled-back parameter $\varpi$ is again a regular parameter. It feeds the corresponding statement phrased directly for a localisation, [`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_isUnramifiedAt_off`](thm.html#IsRegularLocalRing.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_isUnramifiedAt_off), whose purpose is to establish regularity of the quotient by $\varpi$ in the study of the local rings arising from the deformation-theoretic and Hecke-algebra constructions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_of_isInvariant_of_card_inertia_eq_of_isUnramifiedAt_off.lean

